    {
      "start": 119.95,
      "end": 120.88,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Hermana,",
          "en": "Sister — religious title for a nun (here, addressing you).",
          "pron": "Spanish approx.: ayr-MAH-nah. Syllables: Her-ma-na; stress on -MAH-. H as a light aspiration in Spain; in many Americas it is silent (ear-MAH-nah). IPA-style: /eɾˈma.na/ (Spain) or /eɾˈma.na/ with silent h. Pause slightly after the comma before the name."
        },
        {
          "t": "Viridiana.",
          "en": "Viridiana — the novice’s name.",
          "pron": "Spanish approx.: vee-ree-DYAH-nah (Latin American) or bee-ree-DYAH-nah (Spain, soft b/v). Syllables: Vi-ri-dia-na; stress on -DIA-. IPA-style: /bi.ɾiˈðja.na/ or /bi.ɾiˈðja.na/; the ll/y sound is a short “y” glide in most dialects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 125.84,
      "end": 129.28,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "La caridad que practicamos aquí",
          "en": "The charity that we practice here",
          "pron": "lah kah-ree-DAHD keh prahk-tee-KAH-mohs ah-KEE. Word by word: la (LAH); caridad (kah-ree-DAHD, stress -DAD); que (keh, short); practicamos (prahk-tee-KAH-mos, stress -KAH-); aquí (ah-KEE, stress -KEE). Soft Spanish r in caridad; rolled or tapped r in practicamos (first r tapped, second often tapped in -mos)."
        },
        {
          "t": "no debe ser",
          "en": "must not be",
          "pron": "noh DEH-beh sehr. debe (DEH-beh): e as in “bed”; stress on first syllable DE-. ser (sehr): one smooth syllable, Spanish e as in “bed”, rolled r at the end is light."
        },
        {
          "t": "solo abstracta.",
          "en": "only abstract.",
          "pron": "SOH-loh ahb-STRAHK-tah. solo: stress OH; abstracta: stress STRAHK, final -ah clear; z/c before a/o in Latin America often like “s” (ahs-TRAK-tah)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 134.47,
      "end": 152.8,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Antes de profesar,",
          "en": "Before you take (religious) vows / before professing",
          "pron": "AHN-tes deh proh-feh-SAHR. Antes: stress AHN-. de: quick “deh”. profesar: stress -SAHR; r rolls lightly at the end; comma = short pause."
        },
        {
          "t": "quiero que cumplas",
          "en": "I want you to fulfill (subjunctive)",
          "pron": "KYEH-roh keh KOOM-plahs. quiero: stress KYEH-. que: keh. cumplas: KOOM-plahs, stress KOOM-, subjunctive of cumplir; final -s like “s”."
        },
        {
          "t": "una última misión de caridad.",
          "en": "one last mission of charity.",
          "pron": "OO-nah OOL-tee-mah mee-syOHN deh kah-ree-DAHD. última: stress OOL-; misión: stress syOHN with “y” glide; caridad again kah-ree-DAHD."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 155.34,
      "end": 157.75,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Debes ir a la finca",
          "en": "You must go to the country estate / farm",
          "pron": "DEH-bes eer ah lah FEEN-kah. Debes: stress DEH-. ir: eer (like “ear” shorter). a la: ah lah linked. finca: FEEN-kah, stress FEEN-, c like “k”."
        },
        {
          "t": "de tu tío don Jaime.",
          "en": "of your uncle Don Jaime.",
          "pron": "deh too TEE-oh dohn HY-meh. tío: TEE-oh, stress TEE-, í is clear “ee”. don: dohn, low nasal vowel. Jaime: HY-meh (like English “high” without full diphthong + meh)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 158.52,
      "end": 162.97,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Él te ha pedido",
          "en": "He has asked you",
          "pron": "ehl teh ah peh-DEE-doh. Él: stress on ehl (accent shows it’s “he,” not “the”). te: teh. ha: ah. pedido: peh-DEE-doh, stress -DEE-, past participle of pedir."
        },
        {
          "t": "que vayas antes de tomar los votos.",
          "en": "that you go before taking your vows.",
          "pron": "keh BAH-yahs AHN-tes deh toh-MAHR lohs BOH-tohs. vayas: BAH-yahs, subjunctive of ir, stress BAH-. antes: AHN-tes. tomar: toh-MAHR, stress -MAR. los votos: lohs BOH-tohs; votos: BOH-tohs, stress BOH-, plural of voto."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 165.66,
      "end": 169.48,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "No quiero verlo,",
          "en": "I don’t want to see him,",
          "pron": "noh KYEH-roh BEHR-loh. verlo: BEHR-loh, proclitic lo attached to infinitive ver; r slightly rolled; stress BEHR-."
        },
        {
          "t": "madre.",
          "en": "Mother — here, the Mother Superior.",
          "pron": "MAH-dreh. Stress MAH-; dreh with soft Spanish r (single flap) between vowels in many dialects: MAH-dreh."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 173.09,
      "end": 174.75,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Es un acto de humildad",
          "en": "It is an act of humility",
          "pron": "ehs oon AHK-toh deh oo-meel-DAHD. Es: ehs. un: oon. acto: AHK-toh, stress AHK-. humildad: oo-meel-DAHD, stress -DAHD, u like “oo” short."
        },
        {
          "t": "y de perdón.",
          "en": "and of forgiveness / pardon.",
          "pron": "ee deh pehr-DOHN. y: ee (like “ee” in “see,” shorter). perdón: pehr-DOHN, stress -DOHN, ó clear oh, n nasal in many dialects."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 175.95,
      "end": 181.35,
      "words": [
        {
          "t": "Tu tío está solo",
          "en": "Your uncle is alone",
          "pron": "too TEE-oh ehs-TAH SOH-loh. Tu: too. tío: TEE-oh. está: ehs-TAH, stress -TAH, for state/condition. solo: SOH-loh, stress OH."
        },
        {
          "t": "y enfermo de nostalgia.",
          "en": "and ill with nostalgia / longing.",
          "pron": "ee ehn-FEHR-moh deh nohs-tahl-HEE-ah. enfermo: ehn-FEHR-moh, stress -FEHR-. nostalgia: nohs-tahl-HEE-ah, stress -HEE-, written ll/y pronounced as “y” in most dialects."
        }
      ]
    },
